                        "entry_id": "3877a9f5-6da8-3f4c-82be-b747c7228937",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small pork sausage, usually served fried."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e56efe96-274c-40b2-bb7c-b36ceee2ec33",
                                "sense_id": "dcaf09e5-d826-3e52-8587-d1bf95d15325",
                                "text": "Yesterday we had bratwurst for dinner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54720dba-ced9-4049-b5b0-5b63ccdf4c55",
                                "sense_id": "dcaf09e5-d826-3e52-8587-d1bf95d15325",
                                "text": "2012, Lindsey Galloway, (bbc.co.uk) A German enclave in central Texas\nFor just-right spiced bratwurst and sausage, try Opa’s Smoked Meats, a family-owned shop that uses original German recipes passed down the generations and always has samples on hand. Finish off any meal with a stop at Chocolat, one of the few chocolate shops in the US that uses a classic European technique known as “liqueur praliné”, where a delicate sugar casting encases liquor, espresso, wine or other liquid fillings. The casting is then covered in chocolate to make a confection that must be eaten whole, lest the encased liquid come dribbling out."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
